{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-19T20:57:51.806Z","data":{"text":"`compute_seal` is back and passes `cargo test -p osq-core --test seal_compute` (10 tests) and `sh scripts/verify-rust.sh`.\n\nThe mutants step in `verify-rust.sh` didn't run because `OSQ_DIFF` isn't set. I ran `cargo mutants` directly on `seal.rs` and `seal/normalize.rs` instead. It tested 38 mutants: 36 caught, 2 unviable, none missed or timed out. The watcher's own change-level verify wasn't run, so the earlier `change_verify_red` has only been checked this way.\n\nThe worktree had lost attempt 4's code again, so I rewrote it:\n- **Dependency:** `sha2 = \"0.11\"` is in the workspace and `crates/core/Cargo.toml`; `Cargo.lock` is updated.\n- **`compute_seal`:** it sorts entries by UTF-16 code unit order and hashes each path and its normalized content. `lib.rs` re-exports it.\n- **`seal/normalize.rs`:** it holds the content normalization (UTF-8 decoding, CRLF to LF, the `tasks.md` checkbox reset). It uses `take_while` instead of index loops, which is what removes the mutant timeouts from last time.\n- **`no_io.rs`:** it now expects `serde`, `serde_json` and `sha2`, and takes a dotted key's name before the first `.`.\n- **`seal_compute.rs`:** it has one test per table row (rows with the same seal share a test) plus the UTF-16 order case. A further edge test covers the line-start and whitespace cases that the two earlier missed mutants pointed at.\n\nThe result file is at `openspec/changes/223-rust-approval-seal/.run/results/1.md`."}}
